# Parity check: the public postcode lookup service is the source of truth; the local
# API must behave the same way for the same postcode. Run in the IntelliJ HTTP client
# (run the whole file). Each "external" request saves its result via save-external.js;
# the "local" request after it is checked by compare-with-external.js:
#   1. the status codes match;
#   2. on 200 for multiple-addresses, both bodies are arrays and are either both empty
#      or both non-empty (counts are not compared: the local database is only a sample);
#      on 200 for postcode, both bodies are objects with the same fields.
# The local database must be loaded with LU49PJ and WF27QD.
# Not covered: a postcode containing "/" (rejected by the external gateway with 401)
# and a missing postcode parameter (no external equivalent).

@external = https://postcode-lookup.company-information.service.gov.uk
@local = http://localhost:8080/address-lookup-api

### multiple-addresses 'LU49PJ' - external
GET {{external}}/multiple-addresses/LU49PJ

> ./save-external.js

### multiple-addresses 'LU49PJ' - local
GET {{local}}/multiple-addresses?postcode=LU49PJ

> ./compare-with-external.js

### multiple-addresses 'lu49pj' - external
GET {{external}}/multiple-addresses/lu49pj

> ./save-external.js

### multiple-addresses 'lu49pj' - local
GET {{local}}/multiple-addresses?postcode=lu49pj

> ./compare-with-external.js

